{
 "id": 334600,
 "name": "Case created/updated in Salesforce will create/update issue in JIRA",
 "description": "**Recipe details**\nWhenever a case is created or updated in Salesforce,  create or update a corresponding issue in JIRA. \n\nConditions can be added to the trigger to execute this issue creation in JIRA only when the case in Salesforce meets certain criteria.\n\nThis recipe maintains a link between Salesforce cases and JIRA issues by inserting the Salesforce case number into the JIRA issue's description field.\n\n**Required parameters**\n1) From: determine the date from which we should start processing closed priority issues.\n2) Project key: determine which project to create issues under\n3) Issue type: determine which issue type to create the issues as\n\nThe project key and issue type parameters are currently set on a recipe level, i.e. all issues will be created in the same project as the same issue type. To create issues under different projects and as different types, use a lookup table in formula mode. [Learn more about lookup tables here.](https://support.workato.com/support/solutions/articles/1000185431-lookup-tables-to-map-values-across-two-apps-)\n\nChange Log : \n15 / 10 / 2016 - Fixed job report",
 "applications": [
  "salesforce",
  "jira"
 ],
 "action_applications": [
  "jira"
 ],
 "trigger_application": "salesforce",
